                        "review": "A cute and relaxing game with light puzzles and a great soundtrack. As many other reviewers have noted, the combat is quite terrible but thankfully it makes up a pretty small portion of the gameplay. Most of your time will be spent solving fairly simple puzzles. There is no mystery to the story, but it is still a charming concept that is executed well. \n\n [u] Pros [/u]\n[list]\n    [*]Excellent music\n    [*]Charming visuals\n    [*]Relaxing vibes with just enough complexity to the puzzles to keep it engaging\n[/list]\n\n [u] Cons [/u]\n[list]\n    [*]Mediocre voice acting-- some of it was decent but a lot was either cringy or just had some weird emphasis.\n    [*]Clunky combat; the game would have been better if it had remained a pure puzzle game\n[/list]\n\nOverall, I had fun with this little game. If they have improved the combat, then I'd be very interested in checking out the sequel. I'd definitely give this one a try for its music alone, but maybe pick it up on sale.",
